All the scoped suites the PR description claims are indeed green. Now let me do the final exhaustive re-read of the changed portions of the lib file to catch anything else.

Re-reading `_committedOutcome` once more:

```dart
case ErrorEvent():
  final resumable =
      _resumableAbort(event, cancelToken) ||
      _resumableTransportFailure(event, cancelToken);
  if (resumable && run.lastEnded >= 0) {
    return _AbortedPartial(event.error, run.lastEnded + 1, event.reason);
  }
  run.forward(_midAnswer(event));
  return const _Forwarded();
```

Hmm — one more: when `resumable` is true but `lastEnded < 0` (committed via deltas but no completed block), the failure is transport-class → `_midAnswer(event)` → retryable → mid-answer wrap "not retried". Fine (in-flight block drops; deliberate).

And `_replaysAttempt` for the transport class in NON-resume mode pre-commit: replays — pre-existing. In RESUME mode: replays (tail) — right.

One more consideration — `_drive`'s `_AbortedPartial` branch calls `cancelToken?.reset()` unconditionally. For the transport class, the token is guaranteed NOT cancelled (checked in `_resumableTransportFailure`). For the abort class, watchdog-fire only. reset() on a non-cancelled token — is it a no-op? Let me check CancelToken.reset quickly to make sure reset on an open token doesn't corrupt state.

